{"_id":"0C7QgWySV8DwRVY0","name":"Giant Ice Crab","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-ice-crab","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Cold regions, Rivers, Coasts","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"13 (Many Legs) / 13 (Swimming)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"GR, Battle Mastery p.119","description":"This subspecies of giant crabs has adapted to life in cold regions, specifically dwelling in riverbanks and shoals. It is characterized by its white shell and measures approximately 1.5 meters in length. While the shell itself is not very durable, the entire exterior of the crab's body is covered in hair that contains sensory organs. This hairy covering is believed to provide protection against the cold as well.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Icebubble Breath / 6 (13) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Within \"Range: Touch\" it sprays icy bubbles at up to three targets, dealing 2d+3 points of Water/Ice magic damage. This ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nIcy Claw (100G / Red Gold A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 11 |\nIcy Shell (200G / Red Gold A) |\n12+ |\nSnow White Shell (600G / Red Gold A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Ice Crab","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"31RpQ9DioUaqtNsK","name":"Shotel Runner","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:shotel-runner","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands, Shallows","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"13","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"AB, p. 92","description":"This is a monster with a height of 50-60cm and length of 1.2-1.5m, having an appearance between a bird and a lizard. It has a red comb and tail, navy-colored feathers, and one purple hook claw on each side that can grow up to 30cm in length. It was named after these distinctive hook claws which resemble the double-edged curved sword called a Shotel.\n\nIt is omnivorous, and when in groups, they may recklessly attack large animals.\n\nMost of them are found in Shallows, but they are occasionally spotted outside the Shallows as well. Their meat is edible.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"►Double Attack","description":"With two Scythes, it attacks one target twice."},{"title":"⏩Scythe Resonance","description":"Strike its scythe to boost its morale. Using this ability costs 3 HP. For 10 seconds (1 round), gains +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and +2 to damage.\nThis effect can stack up to 2 times (+2 accuracy, +4 damage) while in a Shallow Abyss. It does not stack outside of Shallows.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCheap Meat (100G/Red A) |\n2 - 7 |\nHard Sickle (50G/Red Black B) |\n8+ |\nHard Sickle (50G/Red Black B) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Shotel Runner","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"3eyLTyRa6ziMvl3t","name":"Ametrine Elk","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ametrine-elk","level":8,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands, Frozen Plains, Shallows","reputation":16,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"AB, p. 93","description":"This is a giant moose, standing about 4m tall and 6m long, with an amber-colored right side and a purple left side. It has a rich, silvery mane that gleams. Its antlers spread widely, spanning over 3m from tip to tip. Its large eyes have irises made of multiple black concentric circles that can drive those who meet its gaze into madness. It contains Abyss Shards within its body.\n\nAlthough herbivorous, it is extremely territorial and mercilessly charges at any intruders in its territory.\n\nIt primarily inhabits Shallows, but there have been rare sightings outside the Shallows during full moons and new moons.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨Great Horn Sweep","description":"Choose up to 5 characters that can perform melee attack and execute an attack with the great horn against them. This ability cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"🗨Upward Thrust","description":"Can only be declared when the target has only one section, is bipedal, and is actually standing on the ground with both feet only. When the great horn attack hits, it deals damage and simultaneously knocks prone the target."},{"title":"⏩Eyes of Madness/11(18)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Brings madness to those who meet its gaze.\nAffects \"Target: 1 Entire Character\" within \"Range/Area: Target / 1 (10m).\" If a target fails their Willpower check, during their turn when attempting to use a weapon attack, casting spell, or effect with \"Target: 1 Character\" against this monster, they must roll 1d. On a roll of \"4-6\", they may proceed normally, but on \"2-3\", they must cancel the action. If it was a Major Action, the Major Action opportunity is lost, and if it was a Minor Action, they cannot retry the same action during their turn. On a roll of \"1\", they must randomly change their target (regardless of ally or enemy) within the rules' limitations. If changing the target is impossible by the rules (for example, when making a melee attack when only this monster and the target are in the skirmish area), the action is canceled.\nWhen targeting multiple characters simultaneously through abilities like [Metamagic/Targets] with a \"Target: 1 Character\" spell, a roll of \"2-3\" cancels the entire action. On a \"1\", one target must be changed from this monster to a different character where possible. If such target change is impossible, the action is canceled.\nThis effect is Psychic type and lasts for 10 seconds (1 round). This ability can only be used once per turn outside a Shallow Abyss. However, within a Shallow, it can be used up to twice per turn. Additionally, within the Shallow, affected targets receive a -1 penalty (total minimum 1) to their 1d roll before taking actions.\nCharacters on the battlefield can automatically avoid being targeted by this ability until the start of their next turn by declaring they \"do not look directly at this monster\" at the start of their turn. However, they cannot then use ranged attacks or ranged magic targeting this monster directly. Melee attacks are possible but receive a -2 penalty to Accuracy checks. Additionally, when receiving Melee Attacks from this monster, they must take a -2 penalty to Evasion checks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGlossy Fur (150G/Gold Red A) x 2 |\nAlways |\nFine Meat (200G/Red A) |\n2 - 6 |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) |\n7 - 11 |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) x 2 |\n12+ |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ametrine Elk","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"5FNBXPKTZi7Y2EaZ","name":"Blazing Mammoth","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:blazing-mammoth","level":15,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Volcano","reputation":22,"weakness":25,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":21,"movementSpeed":"25 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"19 (26)","source":"CR III p. 354","description":"This huge elephant-like animal continuously emits fire from its entire body and stands about 6 meters tall. It is adapted to volcanic regions, and the fire on its skin is not emitted from its own body but is ignited by rubbing its body against the surrounding magma to keep the fire going.\n\nWhen angered, they secrete a viscous liquid from their skin, increasing the intensity of their flames.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity","description":"Head"},{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"► Fire Shower/19 (26)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Raising its snout high, it blows fireballs. The fireball deals 2d+25 fire magic damage to \"Target: 1 area(3m Radius/5\" within \"Range: Caster.\"\nThis ability can only be used once every 20 seconds (2 rounds)."},{"title":"► Throw/17 (24)/Evasion/Negates","description":"The Blazing Mammoth attempts to grab a \"Target: 1 Character\" within \"Range: Touch.\" If successful, the target is thrown to the rearguard area of their faction (Simplified Combat) or in any direction chosen by this monster at 30m (Standard Combat) and falls down, taking 45 points of fall damage.\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Blazing Mammoth's height prevents enemies from attacking its head.\nThe Head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. This effect disappears when the Body section falls to 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"► Trample with Both Feet","description":"The Blazing Mammoth may Trample twice during the same turn but must attack two different characters."},{"title":"◯ Flame-clad/Can't","description":"The body surface of the Body section is always covered with fire. Any character in the same position (area, coordinate) as this monster will receive 6 fire magic damage at the end of this monster's turn.\nThis ability is lost when the HP of the Body section becomes less than 0."},{"title":"⏩ Burning Rage","description":"The damage caused by [ ◯ Flame-clad] is increased by +2 points for 3 minutes (18 rounds). This bonus is accumulated up to 3 times (max +6 points).\nTo use this ability, the monster must spend 5 points of HP. Also, it can use this ability only once per round.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nDamaged Ivory Tusk (100G/Gold Red A) |\n9 - 10 |\nRed Ivory Tusk (1,600G/Gold Red S) |\n11 - 12 |\nCrimson Ivory Tusk (3,600G/Gold Red S) |\n13+ |\nCrimson Lotus Ivory Tusk (6,600G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Blazing Mammoth","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"5gsAqb9EXn0Yj9ZY","name":"Poison Toad","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:poison-toad","level":2,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"None","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Earth Damage +3","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs) / 20 (Swimming)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"BM","description":"A giant poisonous toad that has grown to around 1m long. These Poison Toads inhabit a variety of areas, with those in the forests and grasslands taking on a deep green hue, while those who dwell in wetlands and ruins have a color ranging from dark blue to near purple. Numerous warts that cover their body constantly ooze toxins, which can be dangerous to those who wish to prey on these toads. However, pharmacists will buy these toxins and oils for a decent price.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison / 3 (10) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the Slam attack inflicts 1 or more applied damage, it inflicts 6 Poison magic damage to the target.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 10 |\nToad Oil/(20G/Red B) |\n11+ |\nClarified Toad Oil (100G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Poison Toad","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"5icLLdbh7zv06WPW","name":"Kiparithos","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:kiparithos","level":2,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":8,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"30 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla, p. 125","description":"In the Great Sebrae Forest in the Ursyla Region, you can find fish species that fly between the trees using fairy magic. While the most well-known among them is the delicious Flying Fish of the Forest Sea (see p. 38, Natural History of Ursyla ), the Kiparithos is a similar yet distinct magical creature.\n\nThe Kiparithos is notably larger than the Flying Fish of the Forest Sea and incomparably more agile in terms of speed. Its scales, which blend into the branches and leaves by reflecting light, are extremely sharp and can tear through even armor with just a touch during flight.\n\nDuring the breeding season, they tend to form groups and become aggressive, so caution is required. Female Kiparithos, in particular, protect their eggs by coating them with a unique bodily fluid, which is also used to attack predators. Interestingly, when this fluid is sufficiently heated, it develops an indescribable thickness and sweetness, making it a sought-after delicacy.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight","description":"Gain a +1 bonus modifier to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks."},{"title":"⏩Protective Mucus Ejection / Can't","description":"This effect can be attempted once during combat when the Kiparithos' current HP is at or below half of their maximum HP (rounded up).\nWhen attempting to use this effect, the GM immediately rolls 1d. On a result of 1-3, the creature is male, and the effect cannot be used. On a 4-6, the creature is female, and the effect is successfully used.\nWhen the effect is used, body fluid is ejected with \"Range: Caster\" targeting \"1 Area (3m radius) / 5\". If the target is a Kiparithos, their Defense is increased by +1 for 3 minutes (18 rounds). This effect does not stack. If the target is not a Kiparithos, they take 2 points of Poison magic damage."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"Loot Slimy Delicacy cannot be obtained from specimens that attempted to use [⏩Protective Mucus Ejection] and were male (roll 1-3). From specimens that attempted and were female (roll 4-6), exactly 1 piece can be obtained regardless of the loot determination roll.\nFor specimens that did not use this effect during combat, roll 1d again to determine their sex. Results of 1-3 indicate male specimens from which no loot can be obtained. From specimens that roll 4-6, there is a possibility of obtaining 1d pieces.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nSlime Delicacy (60G/Red B) |\n7+ |\nSlime Delicacy (60G/Red B) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Kiparithos","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"70dQ6FLyUawadXij","name":"Petroviper","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:petroviper","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Grassland, Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15(Crawling)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR II p. 356","description":"This is a serpent with a dangerous poison that gradually petrifies its prey. The poison is mainly used to weaken its prey. However, it can also be used as a weapon against powerful enemies, and it will not stop attacking until it has completely petrified its prey.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Petropoison/7 (14)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Bite's attack hits and deals more than 1 point of applied damage, the target will gain the Petrifaction (Dexterity, Agility/-6) effect. This effect is Poison type.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nSnake Skin (20G/Red B) |\n5 - 8 |\nFine Snake Skin (120G/Red A) |\n9+ |\nPremium Snake Skin (320G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Petroviper","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7JcXVZiy7M5BSkCR","name":"Wolf","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:wolf","level":1,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Meadow","reputation":5,"weakness":10,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"1 (8)","source":"CR I p. 410","description":"A simple Wolf, often appearing in packs of 3 to 5.\n\nThey are often tamed by Bolgs .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Wolf","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"AKUQC6lkbBokcT3U","name":"Blade Storm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:blade-storm","level":11,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands, Hills","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Earth Damage + 3 points","initiative":22,"movementSpeed":"40 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"BM","description":"It is a small ferret whose entire body is covered with steel gray body hair. The fur is as sharp as a blade, and can slice through skin just by touching it. The ferret's front paws are covered with stiff hairs that resemble blades. The ferret will attack its prey as it passes by, capturing it when it is vulnerable.\n\nThey are ferocious for their size and will attack large opponents without regard to their size in order to protect their territory.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► 3 Attacks (Flexible)","description":"The monster uses multiple weapons and makes three attacks in one round. After making one attack the monster can choose whether to make the next attack on the same target or on a different target of their choice."},{"title":"◯ Sleeping Poison / 13 (20) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the Paw Blade attack hits, the target is put to sleep. This effect is of the Poison type, and countermeasures against Poison are effective.\nAfter the target falls asleep, the effect is also treated as a Psychic type. It is possible to bring the target back to consciousness with the [ Sanity ] spell. However, since this effect is not a Psychic type (Weak), the target cannot be simply woken up using Major Action.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBroken Paw Blade (400G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 11 |\nWired Hair (870G/Red Black A) |\n12+ |\nSharp Wired Hair (2,880G/Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Blade Storm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ARPppPFd0EqRjxlJ","name":"Megaloceros","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:megaloceros","level":12,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Snowfields","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"22 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"15 (22)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.122","description":"This white-haired deer is revered as the guardian god of the snowfields and hail. From the time they are born, their antlers continue to grow, and by the time they reach adulthood, they are over one meter long.\n\nAs the antlers grow, they become harder and more translucent, giving them a mineral-like appearance. The antlers create cold air around them, and can be wielded to create snowstorms or freeze moisture in the air to form ice cubes.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Adapted to Snow","description":"Megaloceros is not subject to adverse modifications for poor footing due to snow, etc. or cold weather."},{"title":"◯ Ice Deer Rationale","description":"Megaloceros have a lot of experience in combat, and they judge the combat situation correctly and act accordingly.\nIn judging the actions of combat, treat it as \"Intelligence: Average.\""},{"title":"► Summon Snowstorm/15 (22)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Megaloceros swings its antlers in complex gestures, creating a blizzard. This unique skill has \"Range: Caster\" and deals 2d+12 water/ice magic damage to \"Target: 1 area (Radius 6m)/20\".\nIf the value of the target's resistance check for this effect is lower than the value of this unique skill by 3 or more, the target cannot take a Minor Action for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns, and it consumes 10 MP when used."},{"title":"⏩ Ice Shards/16 (23)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Antlers become covered with ice, and it throws it. It deals 2d+14 Water/Ice magic damage to \"Target: 1 Character\" to \"Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot \".\nThis unique skill can only be used once per round, and costs 6 MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nIce Deer Antlers (3,100G/Red S) |\n7 - 12 |\nClear Ice Deer Antlers (7,400G/Red S) |\n13+ |\nCrystallized Ice Deer Antlers (14,800G/Red SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Megaloceros","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"CUABMhq6893omx8y","name":"Crash Bear","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:crash-bear","level":8,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountain","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"2 (19)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 358","description":"These giant bears appear in forests and low mountains. They are known to be fierce and dangerous. They are especially dangerous in the fall before hibernation. Still, suppose they fail to hibernate and are active during the winter. In that case, they can be so dangerous that adventurers must be immediately dispatched to their habitat area.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ 2 Actions","description":"Can perform two Major Actions in one round."},{"title":"◯ Throw","description":"If the Claws attack hits, it slams the target into the ground and causes it to fall prone ."},{"title":"► Fall On / Can't","description":"This ability can only be used if the target is character prone.\nThe target receives 2d+18 physical damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGlossy Fur (150G/Gold Red A) |\n2 - 10 |\nBear Paws (300G/Red A) |\n11+ |\nAromatic Bear Paws (1,200G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Crash Bear","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"DgIs52wQhyMJsPmt","name":"Coast Lizard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:coast-lizard","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Seas, Seaside","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"16 (4 Legs) / 20 (Swimming)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 121","description":"This large lizard is frequently spotted at the seashore. It is well-suited to saltwater environments and can often be seen swimming in shallow waters. Although it can survive in freshwater, it may also migrate upstream beyond brackish water areas in certain cases. These lizards are carnivorous and will attack anything they encounter, often causing damage to seaside towns and villages.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":"2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nCrocodile Skin (200G/Red A) |\n9+ |\nSuperior Crocodile Skin (600G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Coast Lizard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"DhpA5tdCC59WJnge","name":"Nest Guard Pamana Bee","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:nest-guard-pamana-bee","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":9,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 121","description":"Pamana Bees are large bees that inhabit the Farveld Plains in the Burlight Region. They can grow up to 1 meter in length and have a massive body. These bees fly across the plains, primarily collecting nectar and pollen from pamana flowers. They have a vast radius of activity, extending over 10 km.\n\nGenerally, Pamana Bees have a calm temperament. However, some bees, known as Nest Guards, are assigned to protect their nests and mates. These Nest Guards are larger than the others and can be dangerous and aggressive. They accompany their allies during nectar and pollen collection but may attack foreign enemies.\n\nSince Pamana Bees have a wide range of activity, encountering multiple bees at the same time is rare. Usually, only one Nest Guard accompanies the others. If you come across them near their nests, be prepared to face multiple attackers.\n\nThe nectar stored in Pamana Bee nests is highly regarded for its quality. Due to the large size and quantity of the nests, some individuals have found them and made a fortune. However, this task is dangerous and involves fighting off numerous Nest Guards.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight","description":"A Nest Guard Pamana Bee receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯Poison /5 (12) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a Poison Stinger attack hits and deals 1 or more points of applied damage, the target is dealt an additional 7 Poison magic damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7+ |\nThin Wings (120G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Nest Guard Pamana Bee","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"DsXsWESwZKhLbj8j","name":"Rust Worm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rust-worm","level":7,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"20 (Crawling)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 122","description":"This is a variant of the Sandworm which appears in the Ward of Magic Giant in the Burlight Region. Its entire body is covered with red mucus, which is an aggregation of microorganisms that corrode iron, stone, and wood. The Rust Worm sustains itself by ingesting the metabolites of these microorganisms. As a result, its own digestive organs deteriorate, and its mouth remains closed and unable to open.\n\nThe unique \"Red Sandworm Gem\" which can be obtained as loot can be traded as a raw material for Honey Red Jam.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Corrosive Mucus","description":"Weapons that attacked this monster and armor attacked by this monster will be corroded and lost after 24 hours; cleaning them with wine or other alcohol within 24 hours will prevent this effect."},{"title":"◯Heat Madness","description":"When the monster receives a Fire- or Energy-type effect or damage (even if the applied damage is 0), it becomes ferocious. The monster's damage is increased by +4 for 1 minute (6 rounds). This effect is not cumulative."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"When [◯Heat Madness] occurs, the loot determination roll for this monster is modified by +1. This effect is not cumulative, even if it occurs more than once.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nSandworm Gem (150G/Gold Red A) |\n8+ |\nRed Sandworm Gem (900G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rust Worm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"E36B7tUwgO6jDMpS","name":"Missile Dolphin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:missile-dolphin","level":8,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains, Floating Rocks","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Wind damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"-/30 (Flying)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 122","description":"This is a subspecies of the Sky Whale . This smaller species measures less than 10 meters in length. However, it surpasses the common Sky Whale in both flying speed and maneuverability.\n\nThese creatures are carnivorous and ferocious. They will charge at prey or anything they perceive as a threat to their territory, regardless of size or whether it is in the air or on the ground.\n\nIn the floating island of Sandokia in the Burlight Region, the \"Sky Temple\" and \"Noahs\" airships used for trading with the ground have been increasingly rammed by this subspecies, creating a significant problem.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"►Charge / 11 (18) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This ability can be used only on rounds when a Normal Move is made; it charges and Headbutts an enemy as per the Melee Attack, dealing 2d+18 points of physical damage instead.\nBody"},{"title":"◯Flight I","description":"All sections receive a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks. This also applies to [►Charge].\nWhen the Body section HP becomes 0 or less, this ability ends.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2-9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nWind Crystal (1,600G/Gold S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Missile Dolphin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"EtOVvi04PXKU6AeB","name":"Giant Bat","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-bat","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses (Hearing)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Caves","reputation":8,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"BM","description":"Giant Bats are flying mammals that suck blood from animals. Using ultrasonic waves inaudible to humans, the Bat can find its prey by hearing how the waves echo back to it (echolocation), allowing it to fly around and search for prey in darkness.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Giant Bat receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Bloodsucking","description":"If a Bite attack hits, the monster's HP is restored by a value equal to the applied damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBat Wing (30G / Red B) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7+ |\nPurple Jewel (120G / Gold A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Bat","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FGheIa6aXZffULDP","name":"Winged Water Buffalo","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:winged-water-buffalo","level":7,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Wind Damage +3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"35 (4 Legs) / 13 (Flying)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 123","description":"This is a winged buffalo that inhabits the Finoan Prairie in the Dorden region. It has short reddish-brown fur, gently curving big horns, a body length of nearly 3m, and beautiful feathers of the same reddish-brown color as its fur.\n\nThey often move in herds and are generally docile, but become ferocious when protecting themselves or their companions. The destructive power of their charge attack with horns from above is considerable.\n\nThe meat has a strong, gamey flavor with a wild taste, and can be quite delicious depending on the cooking method. However, the most prized part is the wing section, known as \"Buffalo Wings\" and famous as a delicacy. Cattle raised in the Magnoa Steppe Country, famous for its livestock farming, are rumored to be a crossbred between normal cattle and Winged Buffalo.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩△Mobile Flying","description":"Soars into the sky with wings. For 10 seconds (1 round), gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy check and Evasion check for melee attacks.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns. When used during Combat Preparation, it cannot be used in the first round regardless of the Initiative check result."},{"title":"►Horn Uppercut / 8 (15) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Lowers its body and perform a close-range attack with its horn in an upward motion. Deals 2d+12 points of physical damage to the target. Targets who successfully evade this attack must then perform an \"Acrobatics check\" with a Target Number of 14, and if they fail, they fall prone.\nThis ability cannot be used in the same turn as [⏩△Mobile Flying]. Also, [⏩△Mobile Flying] cannot be used in the same turn as this ability."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If an effect of Wind type reduces HP to 0 or less, the loot item \"Crimson Feathers\" will be lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCrimson Feathers (450G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 11 |\nBuffalo Wings (300G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nThick Buffalo Wings (1,300G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Winged Water Buffalo","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FfE9vSP8Mvfkt6RD","name":"Brafotes","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:brafotes","level":9,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"40/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 360","description":"This is a monstrous bird without feathers, with a wingspan of an adult of 7 to 10 meters. It has a reptilian-like body and is said to be a kind of pterosaur. They are ferocious; when they catch their prey, they go on a rampage and kill, pecking it. After the meal, it often becomes a paradise for carrion-eating animals. Such animals can be seen running in flocks on the ground, following this monster bird soaring in the sky.\n\nIts membrane is prized as a material for leather goods.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Gale Breath/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Shot \", it exhales a violent wind in \"1 area (3m Radius) / 5\", dealing 2d+8 wind magic damage to the target.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\nBody"},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • Impossible","description":"Its body hinders attacks on the head.\nThe Head section cannot be attacked, whether melee or ranged. When the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears.\nWing"},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"All sections receive a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nThis unique skill is lost if either Wing section is reduced to 0 or less HP.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nSaurian Membrane (100G/Red A) |\n7 - 12 |\nBlack Membrane (500G/Red A) |\n13+ |\nObsidian Membrane (3,000G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Brafotes","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FmHllzkhBErCT4d2","name":"Shark","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:shark","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ocean","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Slashing damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"20 (Swimming)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Barbarous Tales (2.0 sourcebook), p. 70","description":"Sharks live in clear water and have a strong sense of smell for blood. They quickly hunt down prey once they smell blood, making it difficult to escape.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater","description":"A Shark doesn't receive penalties for moving or taking action in water. However, it can't perform any Action without water.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nJagged Tooth (30G/Red B) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11+ |\nClean Gills (200G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Shark","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"GwutLAOzDcauuL5J","name":"Crocodile","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:crocodile","level":5,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Rivers, Swamps","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)/20(Swimming)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR II p. 355","description":"Crocodiles inhabit murky waters near rivers and swamps where they can hide from prey. Their speed while in water is incredible, and their jaws will crush any game caught within. Once dragged underwater, there is no escape.\n\nIt is said that Superior Crocodile Skins can be used for a number of goods, such as luxury bags and wallets.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":"2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 11 |\nCrocodile Skin (200G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nSuperior Crocodile Skin (600G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Crocodile","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"H11TCRFf80acsYLg","name":"Capture Beetle","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:capture-beetle","level":5,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains, Forests","reputation":12,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"5 (5 Legs) / 20 (Flying)","fortitude":"8(15)","willpower":"5(12)","source":"CO, Battle Mastery p.119","description":"A beetle of over 2m in length. Though they lack horns or pincers, they possess long legs capable of dexterous action. It is possible for them to fly while gripping a human child, and there have been rare incidents where livestock have been abducted.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Capture Beetle receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"► Rock Throwing / 4 (11) / Evasion / Negates","description":"The Beetle grabs a nearby rock and hurls it as an attack. This is treated as a Thrown Weapon attack, and has a \"Range: 1 (10m)\" and a \"Target: 1 Character\", and deals 2d+9 of physical damage.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nBeetle Shell (30G / Red B) |\n6 - 9 |\nGood Quality Shell (150G / Red A) |\n10+ |\nSuperior Shell (750G / Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Capture Beetle","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HGi6QmvJX8YqRwOK","name":"Desert Scorpion","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:desert-scorpion","level":11,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Desert","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"25(Many Legs)/10(in sand)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR III p. 351","description":"This is a giant scorpion that inhabits the deserts of the Alframe continent. Its body length, including the tail, exceeds 10 meters.\n\nThese lords of the desert usually lurk in the depths of the sand. When it recognizes an intruder in its territory, it approaches the intruder from the sand and kills it with a single strike of its deadly tail.\n\nThe shells are valuable as armor and building materials. Still, few people attempt to kill a living Desert Scorpion to steal it, instead obtaining it by searching for its rotting carcass in the desert or by picking up anything that falls by chance.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Many Legs","description":"It is not subject to penalties due to poor footing.\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Hide in the Sand","description":"If the character approaches within 15 meters of Desert Scorpion, if they fail the Danger Sense check with target number 18, they will receive a surprise attack (see CR I, p. 144)."},{"title":"⏩ Dusting Sand","description":"For 10 seconds (1 round), all attacks against all sections of this monster have a -1 penalty on Accuracy checks against them and Evasion checks against attacks from them. Characters with Magic perception are not affected by this.\nTo use its ability, 5 points of HP must be consumed.\nRight Pincer/Left Pincer"},{"title":"🗨 Decoy Attack II","description":"It gains -2 to Accuracy checks, but the damage is increased by +8 on hit.\nIf the declared attack is evaded, the enemy receives a -2 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is cumulative up to -8 but is lost if the target fails an Evasion check even once.\nTail"},{"title":"◯ Dead Angle Attack","description":"If the Body section is the target of a melee attack, an Accuracy check by Tail can be performed instead of an Evasion check of the Body section. See [ Counter ] for the detail of the process, CR II, p. 209. In failure, the Body section suffers damage as with [ Counter ] feat.\nThis ability can only be used once per 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"◯ Poison/13 (20)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Tail attack inflicts 1 or more applied damage, it inflicts 10 Poison magic damage to the target.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nPoison Stinger (100G/Red A) |\n2 - 11 |\nFine Scorpion Shell (250G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nLarge Scorpion Shell (2,200G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Desert Scorpion","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HyVqYQt0M9D4QQLL","name":"Triblade Mantis","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:triblade-mantis","level":9,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Wind Damage +3","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs) / 25 (Flying)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (18)","source":"BM","description":"This mantis has grown abnormally long, up to about 7 meters in length. Its scythe, with its tip, split into three parts, is hard enough to cut through rocks. The wings on its body not only allow it to fly but also weaken its prey by vibrating them.\n\nThey can fly, but only for very short periods of time, and they are also not as flexible and maneuverable as on the ground. Therefore, when hunting prey, they descend to the ground to fight.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Cross Strike / 14 (21) / Evasion / Negates","description":"The Mantis makes a melee attack on 1 Character with both its Left and Right Scythe sections simultaneously, dealing 2d+22 physical damage if successful.\nThis ability cannot be used if either the Left or Right Scythe has already taken a Major Action, and when this ability is used, the Major Action for both Sections is considered to be completed."},{"title":"◯ Deflect","description":"If the Body section is the target of a melee or ranged attack, the Right Scythe or Left Scythe section can defend by repelling the attack. Instead of the Evasion check of the Body, each section performs an Accuracy check and compares the Success Values. If the Success Value is equal to or higher than the opponent's Accuracy check, the section takes no damage. If it fails, the Body section receives a hit without making an Evasion check.\nThis ability can only be attempted once per round per section.\nBody"},{"title":"► Disturbing Buzz / 12 (19) / Willpower / Negates","description":"The Mantis flutters its wings violently and produces an unpleasant sound \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (30m Radius) / All\", disrupting the concentration of all the characters there. This inflicts a -1 penalty to all Skill Checks for those who are affected, and lasts for 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is Psychic type.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGlittering Wing Membrane (340/G / Gold Red A) |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10 - 12 |\nThree-bladed Scythe (840G / Red A) |\n13+ |\nHard Three Bladed Scythe (2500G / Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Triblade Mantis","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"I53qiyd6z61hKY2B","name":"Dolphin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dolphin","level":2,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sea Animal","habitat":"Sea, River","reputation":6,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/25 (Swimming)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR III p. 343","description":"This species of Dolphin grows to around 3m long and is highly intelligent, able to speak its own language. While Dolphins often live in groups out in the seas and open ocean, they will rarely come to the coast and attempt to make contact with Humanoids.\n\nFor the mount version of this animal, see Dolphin (mount) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater","description":"It cannot move outside of the water and cannot act outside of the water, but it does not suffer any restrictions or penalties for actions in the water.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nNothing |\n6 - 9 |\nPearl Fragments (50G/Gold Red B) |\n10+ |\nOcean Pearl (200G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dolphin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"I8TlPFlYGPaiQJKg","name":"Sea Serpent","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sea-serpent","level":8,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Sea","reputation":14,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"15 (Crawling)/30(Swimming)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR III p. 348","description":"A giant ocean snake, a Sea Serpent can measure up to 20m long, causing sailors to believe they had encountered an aquatic dragon. Under normal circumstances, they are solitary monsters, content to eat fish but will attack boats when desperately hungry. There are subspecies of Sea Serpents that can live in freshwater, and some cities have even enshrined a Sea Serpent as the embodiment of a water god.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Specialization","description":"Can move in water without penalties and restrictions. Conversely, all Skill Checks are subject to a -2 penalty on the ground.\nHead"},{"title":"► Fire Breath/9 (16)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Spits out a fireball with \"Range: Caster\" and deals 2d+5 fire magic damage to \"Target: 1 area (4m Radius) / 10\".\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Entanglement II","description":"A successful hit from a Sea Serpent attack entangles the target. Each round, the entangled target is dealt 2d+8 physical damage and makes all Accuracy and Evasion Checks with a -2 penalty.\nThe monster can use [ ◯ Entanglement II] to entangle multiple characters with multiple hits and can attack other characters while entangling.\nWhen one of the targets tries to escape, use the de-bonding rules."},{"title":"◯ Long Body","description":"The Head section can make a Bite attack with \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target \".\nWhen the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"The Sea Serpent's height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSea Serpent Scales (200G/Red A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 12 |\nParasitic Shellfish Husk (200G/Red A) |\n13+ |\nShining Parasitic Shellfish Shell (1,000G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sea Serpent","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KKtMoJNmxsVlhf9l","name":"Pack Leader","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:pack-leader","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Meadow","reputation":8,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"16 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 412","description":"These are the leaders of the wolf pack. They are one size larger than a normal Wolf and much more dangerous. However, the true fear lies in the fact that wolves led by a pack leader move in a more controlled manner than regular ones.\n\nFor novice adventurers, a pack of wolves led by a Pack Leader can be a considerable threat.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Pack Command","description":"Gives a +1 bonus to all Wolves' Accuracy and Evasion checks in the skirmish in which it resides. This effect is not cumulative, even if there are multiple Pack Leaders."},{"title":"🗨 Aimed Attack","description":"When attacking, the Pack Leader can gain a +1 bonus to Accuracy. This ability has no effect on characters equipped with metal armor.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 3 |\nNothing |\n4 - 5 |\nWolf Hide (20G/Red B) |\n6 - 8 |\nHigh-quality Wolf Hide (50G/Red B) |\n9+ |\nFlawless Wolf Hide (100G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Pack Leader","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"LFKIHCkX2q8kIGuP","name":"Rushpecker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rushpecker","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"3/19 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CO","description":"With a wingspan of about 50cm, this bird resembles a woodpecker. It is known for its carnivorous nature, pecking at anything and everything it sees as food.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Rushpecker receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"► Triple Attack","description":"Thrusts its beak forward at high speed, attacking one character three times.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHard Beak (60G / Red Black B) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 |\nFlight Feathers (100G / Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rushpecker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"LN3x1HbjzSfilelk","name":"Spotted Bog Rhino","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:spotted-bog-rhino","level":12,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Swamps","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs) / 20 (Swimming)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"BM","description":"A subspecies of the Spotted Rhino , this is a very large aquatic rhinoceros that can grow up to 7 meters in length. The skin is still spotted, but the shading is more distinct.\n\nThey prefer to live in places where the flow is stagnant. When they digest food in their bodies, they produce a foul-smelling gas that they disperse and contaminate their surroundings.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Charge / 14 (21) / Evasion / Negates","description":"The Spotted Bog Rhino runs forward with \"Range/Area: 2(45m) / Breakthrough \" dealing 2d+22 physical damage and knocking them prone.\nTo use this ability, the Spotted Bog Rhino must be able to make a Full Move, and all Sections of its body must be capable of making Major Actions. The use of this ability is declared before the movement, and once it has taken place, all Sections are considered to have taken their Major Actions and the Rhino suffers a -4 penalty to its Evasion for the next 10 seconds (1 round).\nHead"},{"title":"► Stinky Breath / 14 (21) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Spotted Bog Rhino exhales a strong odor with \"Range/Area: 2(20m) / Shot \" in \"Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5\", dealing 2d+16 Poison magic damage to the target. In addition, the target who fails the resistance is overwhelmed by the smell for 1 day and suffers a -2 penalty for all Skill Checks that use the Intelligence modifier for Standard Value calculation. This effect is lost if the target washes their entire body with water for 1 hour.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\nBody"},{"title":"► Kick Away/14 (21)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Kicks \"Target: 1 Character\" at \"Range: Touch.\" The target will be moved one area to the rear of the Rhino (Simplified Combat) or 20m in an arbitrarily determined direction (Standard/Advanced Combat). The victim receives 20 falling damage and will be knocked prone."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"A Spotted Rhino's height prevents enemies from attacking it. The head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Body section HP falls to 0 or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBroken Big Horn (630G/Red A) |\n2 - 6 |\nSpotted Skin (190G/Red A) |\n7+ |\nSlimy Skin (680G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Spotted Bog Rhino","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"LOn7nI49hjEOtUBP","name":"Giant Eagle","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-eagle","level":7,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wastelands, Mountains","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"-/30(Flying)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.113","description":"This huge eagle is 3 meters in length and over 5 meters in height. It preys on animals as large as a human adults by weakening them with its sharp claws and taking them to its nest.\n\nSometimes flying Barbarous train them and keep them as pets.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Giant Eagle receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"🗨 Dive Attack","description":"The Giant Eagle dives down from a high altitude down on the unsuspecting prey.\nThe Accuracy check is increased by +2, and the damage increases by 4 points. As a risk, the Giant Eagle receives a -3 penalty on the Evasion checks.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nFeathers of the Bird of Prey (400G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Eagle","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"LiS3gBTUqlYk1iW3","name":"Marsavra","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:marsavra","level":10,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Grasslands","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Water/ice damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR III p. 350","description":"This large, fat, balloon-like reptile inhabits the south-central part of the Alframe continent. It is about 8 meters long and prefers arid land, but its body surface resembles that of a crocodile and is also covered with hard scales. Some call it crocodile skin, but it is superior to crocodile skin and is used as a material for leather products.\n\nWith a voracious appetite, any animal they see is prey for them, as large as a horse. When they find their prey to be a threat, they will spit out the fire to weaken it, and then, bouncing their whole body, they will try to finish it off.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Body Press/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"The Marsavra's body leaps up, carrying all the weight on its belly.\nAll characters in the skirmish it resides are dealt 2d+18 physical damage.\nTo use this ability, all sections (Head, Body, and Tail) must be able to make a Major Action, and at least one must perform a Major Action. Then, the Major Action of all sections is completed when this ability is used.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\nHead"},{"title":"► Fire Breath/13 (20)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Spits out a fire mass at \"Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot \", dealing 2d+12 Fire magic damage to \"Target: 1 Character\".\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\nBody"},{"title":"► Potbelly Defense (Attack Obstacle = Impossible • +4)","description":"Extends belly to prevent attacks on the head. For 10 seconds (1 round) after this ability is used, the Head section cannot be the target of melee attacks and gains a +4 bonus on Evasion checks against ranged attacks.\nTail"},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If the section successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nCrocodile Skin (200G/Red A) |\n7 - 9 |\nSuperior Crocodile Skin (600G/Red A) |\n10+ |\nPerfect Crocodile Skin (2,200G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Marsavra","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Lwftjw5sS5Z5qW4h","name":"Sharp Nails","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sharp-nails","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"VC","description":"This monkey species is small, measuring about 70 cm in length. It has long, thin claws on both hands, which it uses to pounce on and attack its prey.\n\nThese monkeys are brutal and vigilant, and they can be tricky, challenging, and distracting as they rip through their prey.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Just Scratches","description":"If the roll of the damage decision is 5 or less, the Sharp Nails gets a +1 bonus to Evasion checks for the following 10 seconds (1 round).\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nThin Nails (120G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sharp Nails","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"M0T0aoAnh4B7Ow54","name":"Tyrant Regilex","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tyrant-regilex","level":18,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Wasteland, Plains, Grasslands","reputation":19,"weakness":23,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":24,"movementSpeed":"35","fortitude":"24 (31)","willpower":"22 (29)","source":"CR III p. 355","description":"Known as the \"tyrant king,\" Tyrant Regilex is an extremely ferocious predator. It stands erect and looks like a lizard with well-developed back legs. They are about 10 meters long, and when they see their prey, they attack without hesitation, no matter how big or small the prey is. Their sharp claws and fangs are their most powerful weapons, and they are uncontrollable once they start rampaging. They are also known as the strongest predators in all Raxia.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Might of the Tyrant/23 (30)/ Willpower/Negates","description":"This unique skill is treated as an effect of \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (100m Radius) / Space\".\nAll characters in the area of effect, except the Tyrant Regilex itself, must perform a Willpower check at the beginning of their turn. If they fail, they suffer a -2 penalty on all action checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round) due to instinctive fear.\nThis effect is of the Psychic type."},{"title":"◯ Enormous Body","description":"Tyrant Regilex's body is too large. Some attacks will not reach the enemy in front of it. The Tail section melee attacks cannot be used to attack targets that have been attacked by Head or Body sections. The reverse is also true.\nHead"},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Tyrant Regilex successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack against the same target."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +20 points.\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Claws","description":"If the Claws attack hits, it should make two damage decisions, dealing them both to the target."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • +4","description":"The giant body hinders attacks.\nThe Head section gains a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee and ranged attacks.\nThis effect disappears when the Body section falls to 0 HP or lower.\nTail"},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike III","description":"They can deal an additional +20 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSharp Fangs (200G/Red A) x 2d |\n2 - 6 |\nGiant Fangs (1,500G/Red S) |\n7 - 12 |\nTyrant Fang (4,200G/Red S) |\n13+ |\nTyrant King Fang (11,700G/Red SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tyrant Regilex","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"NK06iD0PdzxDuiOT","name":"Red Helm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:red-helm","level":10,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"DL","description":"The Korgana region is home to a huge bear that measures over 3 meters in length. Its body fur is almost blackish gray, and the area around its head and shoulders is discolored reddish black from the fresh blood of its prey.\n\nThese bears are extremely ferocious and belligerent. They will attack any creature that unknowingly enters their territory as prey.\n\nThere have been numerous reports of Humanoid and Barbarous beings killed, and surrounding villagers warn travelers and merchants to flee as fast as possible if they find traces of these bears.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ All-Out Attack","description":"A Head can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty."},{"title":"⏩ Cowering Eyes/12 (19)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Stares at one character in close proximity, filling them with fear.\nOne character in the same skirmish area receives a -2 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion checks for 10 seconds (1 round), and the physical and magical damage it inflicts is reduced by 4 points.\nThis effect is Psychic type. This effect can only be used once per 10 seconds (1 round).\nBody"},{"title":"► Double Attack","description":"Can attack twice with the Paws of both hands."},{"title":"◯ Bear Hug","description":"If the Red Helm successfully hits with [ ◯ Double Attack], it will hold the target, and the target will not be able to move or make a melee or ranged attack. Each round, the held target is hit automatically by the Red Helm, dealing 2d + 24 damage.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use the de-bonding rules.\nWhile entangled by this unique skill, the Red Helm cannot attack other characters. If the monster itself wants to release the target, it can do so with a Minor Action."},{"title":"⏩ Intimidating Posture","description":"Stands up and spread their arms wide to intimidate the target.\nFor 10 seconds (1 round), the Head section gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks for melee attacks and +2 damage. At the same time, the Body section takes a -2 penalty to its Evasion checks.\nThis effect can only be used once in 10 seconds (1 round).\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBright Red Fur (1,200G/Red S) |\n2 - 9 |\nBear Paws (300G/Red A) x 2 |\n10+ |\nAromatic Bear Paws (1,200G/Red S) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Red Helm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"OZTZdbX64I1MPWT8","name":"Filthy Rat","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:filthy-rat","level":1,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":6,"weakness":9,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"BM","description":"These rodents are about 40cm long and are found in abandoned buildings and ruins. They propagate in sewer systems and catacombs and are hated by people because they make their homes unsanitary and spread diseases.\n\nThey breed prolifically, and if you see one, it is safe to assume that there are many more around.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Disease Bite / 2 (9) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a character is hit with a Bite attack that inflicts 1 or more applied damage, this character gains a -1 penalty to their Fortitude. This effect is of the Disease type, it is permanent unless healed and it is not cumulative."},{"title":"◯ Nimble","description":"Filthy Rat gains a +2 bonus to the Evasion check against ranged attacks.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11+ |\nDirty Teeth (50G / Red B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Filthy Rat","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"P6OqUOcm5enxHB6E","name":"Swamp Worm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:swamp-worm","level":12,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Swamp","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"10(Crawling)","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR II p. 363","description":"This is a giant earthworm that inhabits the swamps of the Alframe continent. The length of the body, from the mouth to the tip of the tail, is about 20 meters, with the largest exceeding 30 meters.\n\nIt is said that when they leave the swamp where they were born while still young and move to a spring or pond filled with fresh water, they dig up the bottom of the water and turn it into a muddy swamp, making it their new home.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"◯ Swamp Monster Body","description":"Damage from bludgeoning weapons is treated as if Defense were 5 points higher.\nMouth"},{"title":"◯ Bloodsucking","description":"If the Mouth attack hits, the HP of any one section of this monster is recovered by a value equal to the applied damage. Which section is recovered can be selected after each attack and after all the damage determination processes are completed. However, the section with HP below 0 cannot be selected.\nBody"},{"title":"► Fluid Eruption / 16 (23) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"With \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5\", it spurts out bodily fluids to blind the target.\nIf the target fails resistance, it becomes blind. This state can be removed with an effect that cures blindness or by the target wiping its face with Major Action.\nThis unique skill can only be used when the HP of the Body section is less than half of the maximum value (rounded up), and when used, it consumes 10 HP. The body section can lower its HP to 0 or lower, with this ability becoming disabled.\nTail"},{"title":"► Foot Scooping / 12 (19) / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"Its tail crawls underground and attacks the feet of the target. With \"Range: Touch,\" Tail makes up to 5 characters fall prone . This effect only applies to bipedal characters with only one section.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nMud Stone (100G/Gold Black A) |\n7 - 11 |\nBrown Mud Stone (200G/Red Black A) |\n12+ |\nBlack Mud Stone (1,600G/Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Swamp Worm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"P8FBOiPoIsX170J1","name":"Twin Head Falcon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:twin-head-falcon","level":10,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Wind damage +3 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"10/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Natural History of Ursula p. 126","description":"This is a gigantic bird of prey with two heads, mainly spotted in the Tamir Mountains in the Ursyla Region. With a wingspan exceeding 5m, it sometimes preys on humans and horses.\n\nApart from its size and having two heads, its ecology is not much different from normal birds of prey. It has been suggested that this mutation is likely influenced by a Shallow Abyss.\n\nThe large feathers obtained from this monster are highly popular as materials for the \"Wind-cutting Spear\" (see Natural History of Ursula p. 36).","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Painful Strike","description":"If the result of the 2d damage roll is 10 or higher, increase the damage by an additional +8 points.\nBody"},{"title":"◯Flight","description":"All sections gain a +1 bonus modifier to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks. This ability is lost if the Body section's HP falls to 0 or below."},{"title":"🗨Full-Body Strike","description":"Increase damage by +8. As a risk, take a -3 penalty modifier to its own Evasion checks."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"|"},{"roll":"6 - 11","loot":"|"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Twin Head Falcon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Q5KrjPWrHoWbRaws","name":"White Gold Liger","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:white-gold-liger","level":10,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"BM","description":"This is a mutation of the Liger with a white gold mane. With a light step that does not match its huge body, it looks for a gap between the enemies and pounces at once to kill its prey.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Fast Action","description":"During the first round of combat, if the Liger won the initiative, it may take two Major Actions that round."},{"title":"►Triple Attack","description":"The Liger can bite and attack twice with its claws making 3 attacks per round with Bite and Claws."},{"title":"►On Guard","description":"The White Gold Liger stays low and prepares to be attacked by the enemy, gaining a +2 bonus to Evasion checks for 10 seconds (1 round). In addition, on its next turn, it gains a +2 bonus to Accuracy.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nLarge Fang (100G / Red A) x2 |\n2 - 10 |\nLion's Mane (150G / Red A) |\n11+ |\nWhite Gold Mane (1,900G / Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"White Gold Liger","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"RGz8aExnshOwJpht","name":"Liger","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:liger","level":8,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":13,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"BM","description":"It is a crossbred born from the mating of a Lion and a Tiger . They have the stripes of a tiger and the mane of a lion ,and are so large that they can weigh twice as much as their parents.\n\nLigers are rarely fertile and rarely have offspring with lions, tigers, or even with other ligers. It is also unlikely that Lions and Tigers will naturally mate, and they are usually never seen together.\n\nHowever, there are constant reports of Ligers being seen in the Barbarous territories. Apparently, the Barbarous are conducting various breeding experiments, and the Liger seems to be one of such experiments. It is also considered a sighting report because the work of creating Ligers is still being carried out.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fast Action","description":"During the first round of combat, if the Liger won the initiative, it may take two Major Actions that round."},{"title":"► Triple Attack","description":"The Liger can bite and attack twice with its claws making 3 attacks per round with Bite and Claws.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nLarge Fang (100G / Red A) x2 |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nLion's Mane (150G / Red A) |\n11+ |\nGolden Mane (900 G / Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Liger","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"SG3HWfsWga7TtuOw","name":"Grey Lynx","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:grey-lynx","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountain","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"16 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 412","description":"This large wildcat has grown to a size of 2m. The Grey Lynx is keen on hiding itself and avoids Human-sized prey, which leads children to think of these cats as myths.\n\nWhile fur is not quite a luxury, there is still a steady enough demand for it. There may also be seeds from unknown plants stuck in the fur, some of which may yet still sprout.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Grey Lynx successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGrey Lynx Fur (80G/Red B) |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nMysterious Seeds (100G/Red Green A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Grey Lynx","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"SlwP79Qz1wNhLOrw","name":"Purple Ant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:purple-ant","level":2,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountain, Cave, Grassland, Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":8,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12 (6 Legs)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 411","description":"These giant ants are more than 1 meter long and covered with a purple shell. Carnivorous, they nest here and there in Alframe, and their ferocity in attacking at random makes them a threat to people.\n\nThey are often seen in Shallow Abysses, and their nests can be found where Shallows were found before. Abyssal shards are also sometimes found in the nests, and their connection to Abyss is being investigated.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Formic Acid/4 (11)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"Spit acid on \"Target: 1 Character\" at \"Range: Touch,\" dealing 2d-1 poison magic damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nBeetle Shell (30G/Red B) |\n10 - 11 |\nViolet Jewel (120G/Gold A) |\n12+ |\nAbyss Shard (200G) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Purple Ant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VZlMMlb21iBG6rK4","name":"Dark Sweeper","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dark-sweeper","level":5,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Lakes, Swamps","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"16(Many Legs)/16(Swimming)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"KF","description":"This is a giant water spider about 2 meters long. Although it can swim underwater, its main means of transportation is to walk on the water using its water-repellent legs dexterously.\n\nThey nest under bridges or underground in places where water flows and prey on fish and other aquatic animals.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Slime Vomit/6 (13)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Up to \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Shot ,\" this beast spits out a mass of water mixed with a sticky substance to attack \"Target: 1 Character,\"\nThe target suffers 2d+5 Water/Ice magic damage and takes a -2 penalty on Evasion checks for a total of 3 minutes (18 rounds). The penalty to Evasion check is not cumulative and is removed if the target wipes off the sticky water with a Major Action.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nSticky Water (200G/Red A) |\n11+ |\nVery Sticky Water (680G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dark Sweeper","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"XuYy4ooYcWa37vhH","name":"Hammerhead","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hammerhead","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"11 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"GR, Battle Mastery p.118","description":"A quadrupedal animal with a large and rigid head, resembling that of a small rhinoceros in overall shape. These creatures are gentle and live in herds in different locations. They have an omnivorous diet and will consume almost anything. During territorial disputes, they surround their enemies and use headbutts as a form of attack.\n\nHowever, they are not physically strong and are not suitable for domestic tasks such as pulling carts.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nRocky Hide (120G / Red A) |\n11+ |\nFine Quality Rocky Skin (320G / Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hammerhead","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"XwxfKJNAdYSHpMrY","name":"Anaconda","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:anaconda","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Plains, Caves","reputation":8,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"15(Crawling)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR III p. 343","description":"A large snake, an Anaconda measures around 2m in length. Its preferred method of attack is to hide in trees as though it were a large vine, then drop down onto unsuspecting prey. The coils of an Anaconda can constrict and suffocate something as large as a cow. The skin of the Anaconda is prized for its capabilities when turned into leather, and adventurers are often sent to procure such skins.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Entanglement","description":"A successful hit from a Constrict attack entangles the target. In each round, the Anaconda hits the entangled target automatically and makes all Accuracy and Evasion Checks with a -2 penalty.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use the de-bonding rules.\nWhile entangled by this unique skill, the Anaconda cannot attack other characters. If the monster itself wants to release the target, it can do so with a Minor Action.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nSnake Skin (20G/Red B) |\n6 - 9 |\nFine Snake Skin (150G/Red A) |\n10+ |\nPremium Snake Skin (320G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Anaconda","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YHMus4j0FGTWvZfX","name":"Vulture","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:vulture","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains, Forests","reputation":9,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"-/30(Flying)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.108","description":"A large bird of prey that typically lives in high mountains or canyons, the vulture has a wingspan that can reach up to 3 meters. With this, it can easily carry away both livestock and Humans. Normally, vultures are content to fly high above, but when hungry, they will descend to catch prey and bring it back to their nest.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nFlight Feathers (100G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nCheap Meat (100G/Red A) |\n9+ |\nFine Meat (200G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Vulture","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"aULD5ICm7fHg5ga9","name":"Lion","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lion","level":5,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"BM","description":"This fierce four-legged feline carnivore is known as the king of all beasts. They hunt in small groups, setting up territories in grasslands and plains. The males have a magnificent mane, which is highly prized.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Lion successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target."},{"title":"◯ Coordination","description":"A Lion gains a bonus to their Accuracy equal to the number of other Lions in the same skirmish area, up to a maximum of +4.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nLarge Fang (100G / Red A) |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10 - 12 |\nLion's Mane (150G / Red A) |\n13+ |\nGolden Mane (900G / Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lion","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"alNWHFRURq6DVYfJ","name":"Giant Lizard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-lizard","level":2,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":7,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 411","description":"A carnivorous reptile about 2m long. Adventurers should be wary of lone Giant Lizards, as their companions tend to wait in ambush for unwary stragglers.\n\nIn rare cases, there are those specimens with finer scales than usual. If enough of these scales can be harvested and brought to a skilled armorsmith, high-quality scale mail can be made.\n\nFor the mount version of this monster, see Giant Lizard (mount) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Lizard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"cPLI5miSTfWdYBQQ","name":"Fossil Chrysalis","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:fossil-chrysalis","level":7,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"10(Crawling)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR III p. 347","description":"This gigantic chrysalis, about 3 meters long, is often found in old ruins. Because of its huge size, when it is found, it is often only exposed partly in a ruin's room, and its full extent is rarely revealed.\n\nThe body surface of the chrysalis is so hardened that it could be mistaken for a mineral. Moreover, it can move while still in its pupal state, making it dangerous to be caught in its movement. Black tentacles extend from the tip of the chrysalis, and while the body remains motionless, the chrysalis uses the tentacles to defend itself.\n\nIt is said that they hatch when some conditions are met, but there is no reported case of witnessing the moment of hatching.\n\nThey never appear alone but are always surrounded by several to a dozen Crimson Maggots living in symbiosis.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Block","description":"The same as [ Block ] Combat Feat (see CR II, p. 202).\nChrysalis"},{"title":"◯ Chrysalis Body","description":"It is immune to critical hits from edged weapons and slashing-type attacks. It also reduces all magic damage it suffers by -6 points."},{"title":"► Soporific Scent/9 (16)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"It releases a soporific scent, putting all the characters in the skirmish it resides to sleep.\nPoison and psychic (weak) type countermeasures are effective against this effect (for example, this effect can be removed with damage to HP or MP). If the target is protected or resistant to both types, the target may choose either type.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\nTentacle"},{"title":"🗨 △ Cover I (Chrysalis only)","description":"Has the combat feat [ Cover I ] (see CR I, p. 256). The Cover is limited to the Chrysalis section."},{"title":"◯ Long Tentacles","description":"It can attack with Tentacle with \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target \".\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nFossil Shell (300G/Red Black A) x 1d |\n2 - 10 |\nTentacle (220G/Red A) |\n11+ |\nExtended Tentacle (660G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Fossil Chrysalis","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dBZT6YKk6X0qiqLp","name":"Plain Centipede","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:plain-centipede","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Plains","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"20 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR II p. 356","description":"This is a giant centipede that appears on the plains of the Alframe continent. It mainly feeds on animals on the plains, but in the Dorden region, it has been observed to frequent the vicinity of railroad tracks. Studies have shown that they move along the tracks by licking the track water and oil spilled by trains, earning them the nickname \"Railway Centipedes.\" This habit is thought to be a way for them to replenish some nutrients, but this has not been proven with certainty. Because they are quite large, they often block railroad tracks and are requested to be taken down.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Plain Centipede (mount) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Deadly Poison/8 (15)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Jaw attack hits and deals at least 1 applied damage, it deals an additional 2d+6 Poison magic damage to the target.\nBody"},{"title":"🗨 Decoy Attack I","description":"It gains -2 to Accuracy checks, but the damage is increased by +2 on hit.\nIf the declared attack is evaded, the enemy receives a -1 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is cumulative up to -4 but is lost if the target fails an Evasion check even once.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 11 |\nGood Quality Shell (150G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nSuperior Shell (750G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Plain Centipede","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dKjthV3AElZ1El8y","name":"Mega Vice Beak","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:mega-vice-beak","level":7,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"25","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Natural History of Ursula p. 126","description":"This is a flightless giant bird with a long, thick orange beak that can reach 70-80cm in length. Its wings are small compared to its body and are only used to assist in jumping.\n\nIt is omnivorous, feeding on nuts, soft-bodied leaves, and small animals, but when hungry, it is known to attack animals up to its own size.\n\nThe coordination between its legs and beak is characteristic of this bird's hunting style. It earned the name \"Vice\" because it kicks down its prey, clamps it with its beak, and never releases its grip until the prey is completely subdued.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Vise Grip","description":"When the Beak attack hits, it clamps down on the target. The target becomes unable to move and cannot make melee or ranged attacks. Additionally, from the next turn, attacks against the target from the Head section have \"Resistance: Can't\" and deal 2d+20 damage points. When the target attempts to escape, they follow the de-bonding rules .\nWhile a target is clamped by this ability, the Head section cannot attack other characters, and the Body section cannot attack the clamped character. If this monster wishes to release the target, it can do so automatically as a Minor Action.\nBody"},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Size hinders attacks. The head section gains a +4 bonus modifier to Evasion checks against melee attacks. This effect is lost if the Body section's HP falls to 0 or below."},{"title":"◯Throw","description":"When the Kick attack hits, it slams the target to the ground, causing them to fall prone.\nAll Sections"},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If taking even 1 point of Fire damage during combat, the loot Large Feathers cannot be obtained.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCheap Meat (100G/Red A) |\nAlways |\nLarge Feathers (200G/Red A) |\n2 - 9 |\nHard Beak (60G/Red Black B) |\n10+ |\nBig Beak (600G/Red Black A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mega Vice Beak","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"eJrYP2cZIMm7wREu","name":"Grand Coast Lizard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:grand-coast-lizard","level":9,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Seas, Seaside","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs) / 25 (Swimming)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 122","description":"Among the Coast Lizards , this particular individual possesses exceptional vitality and hunting abilities, growing significantly larger than others. It is a dangerous specimen.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"🗨Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 3 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nCrocodile Skin (200G/Red A) |\n9+ |\nSuperior Crocodile Skin (600G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Grand Coast Lizard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gaQbvP9z1HSSjPxW","name":"Hammerhead Leech","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hammerhead-leech","level":2,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"None","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Swamps, Marshes, Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":6,"movementSpeed":"8 (Crawling)","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"AB, p. 92","description":"It is a translucent light purple leech with a T-shaped head, growing to 30-50cm in length. While rarely seen in swamps and wetlands, it is frequently spotted regardless of terrain in Shallow Abysses.\n\nThe semi-transparent body makes it difficult to detect, posing a risk of surprise attacks. Especially in Shallows, it can blend in with surrounding colors, demonstrating enhanced stealth capabilities.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Soft Body","description":"Against damage from blunt weapons, treat Defense as 3 points higher. Cannot be targeted by \"Throw\" or similar attack methods."},{"title":"◯Bloodsucking","description":"When a Bite attack hits, this monster recovers HP equal to the damage dealt."},{"title":"◯Hard to Detect / 10 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"It lurks with its hard-to-see body, waiting for an opportunity. When approaching within 10m of a Hammerhead Leech, failing a Danger Sense check with Target Number 10 results in being surprised.\nWithin a Shallow Abyss, detection becomes even more difficult, and the Target Number for Danger Sense checks becomes 12.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nMucus (20G/Red B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hammerhead Leech","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gius3qOkE31EJNFC","name":"Luana Giant Toad","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:luana-giant-toad","level":3,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Swamps, Riversides","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs) / 10 (Swimming)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 122","description":"This is a giant toad about 1.5 meters long that inhabits Great Luana Lake and its tributaries in the Dorden Region. It secretes a slimy poison liquid from its skin, and hunts by extending its tongue surprisingly far to entangle prey, pulling it in, and weakening it with the skin's poison. While Humanoids tend to be too large as prey, these toads tend to become aggressive towards those who enter their territory.\n\nThe skin's poison liquid is highly traded as it can be refined and formulated into medicine if done skillfully. Additionally, if the skin is carefully removed, the hind legs can be eaten, and there are dedicated enthusiasts for this delicacy.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":"There are no restrictions or penalties for actions in water."},{"title":"🗨Wrap Tongue","description":"It attacks by wrapping around with its long tongue. The tongue attack gains a +1 bonus to the Accuracy check and increases the damage by +2. When this ability is declared, it is treated as having -2 lower Defense for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability is used for attacks whenever possible if HP is above half. On the other hand, when HP falls below half, it can no longer be used."},{"title":"◯Poisonous Skin / 4 (11) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"A target that deals physical damage to this monster through a melee attack must attempt a resistance check against this ability after the damage resolution is complete. If they fail, they take 1d poison magic damage."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If its HP drops to 0 or less while its Defense is reduced by [🗨Wrap Tongue], the loot item \"Poison Frog Fluid\" will be lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nPoison Frog Fluid (90G/Red B) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 11 |\nSturdy Hind Legs (160G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nThick Hind Legs (460G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Luana Giant Toad","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hv2t0s2damOQT2Yy","name":"Forest Kong","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:forest-kong","level":7,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forest","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR II p. 357","description":"This giant ape is found in forests throughout the Alframe continent. They are about 2m 50cm long, and their arms are more developed than their legs. They use their arms and legs to move more quickly than they look. They are so strong that they can easily snap off an ordinary tree with their arms.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ △ Swinging","description":"This beast hangs from a branch or other object above its head. The monster receives no penalty due to poor footing until the beginning of the next turn. It also gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and has its Damage reduced by -2 points.\nThis ability can only be used in environments with something to hang overhead, such as a forest.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nFur (150G/Red A) |\n7+ |\nFine Fur (450G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Forest Kong","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"i1mpgkdmiL1vQJf0","name":"Sabertooth Tiger","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sabertooth-tiger","level":7,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Plains, Forests, Mountains","reputation":14,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 357","description":"Similar in appearance to a regular tiger , the Sabertooth Tiger has two enormous, very sharp canine teeth that give it its name. These fangs are strong enough to easily penetrate metal armor.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Double Bite","description":"When dealing damage with a Claws attack, the damage is rolled twice and added during damage calculation."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nFangs (100G/Red A) x 2 |\n7 - 12 |\nSharp Fangs (200G/Red A) x 2 |\n13+ |\nShining Fang (600G/Gold Red A) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sabertooth Tiger","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"iYXtPGpdk15Mtm4U","name":"Huge Saw Spider","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:huge-saw-spider","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Shallows","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"16 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"AB, p. 93","description":"This is a giant crustacean over 2m in length with dark purple mottled patterns. True to its name \"Huge Saw,\" the two legs positioned in front of its mouth are large and sharp like saws. While it's named \"Spider,\" it's actually not a spider. It has a sea spider-like appearance with spines all over its body and 12 legs. The longest legs reach over 4m. The hard exoskeleton is also quite unlike what you'd find on a spider.\n\nAs its appearance suggests, it is carnivorous and has the strength to easily catch and carry large livestock such as cattle and horses. It may contain an Abyss Shard within its body.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"►Double Attack","description":"It attacks with Saw Legs one target twice."},{"title":"◯Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 9 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +4 points."},{"title":"⏩Purple Mist Spray","description":"When using this effect, consume 6 HP points. Within \"Range: Caster\" and \"1 Area (5m radius)/Space\", sprays a purple bodily fluid like a thin mist.\nFor 10 seconds (1 round), characters with \"Perception: Five Senses\" and \"Perception: Mechanical\" within the effect range receive a -1 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion checks. Within a Shallow Abyss, the penalty becomes -2. This effect does not stack.\nAll Huge Saw Spiders are immune to this effect.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBeetle Shell (30G/Red B) x 2d |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nAbyss Shard (200G/-) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Huge Saw Spider","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ivNQ7DjXRoTxX8XV","name":"Iron Turtle","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:iron-turtle","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Seas, Coasts, Rivers, Swamps","reputation":12,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)/30(Swimming)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 111","description":"This large turtle, ranging anywhere from 1 to 3 m in size, gets its name because its shell is as hard as iron. These turtles are fairly docile, slow to move, and unlikely to cause any harm. However, because their shell is used in a variety of crafts, overfishing has led to a decline in their population and the Iron Turtle is becoming harder to find in the wild.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Shell Guard","description":"The Iron Turtle can retract into its shell, increasing its Defense by +10 for 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"🗨 △ Cover I","description":"The effect is the same as the combat feat [ Cover I ] (see CR I, p. 255).\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nSturdy Shell (200G/Red A) |\n9+ |\nHigh-Quality Shell (1,200G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Iron Turtle","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lG9HA78HHifAgBV3","name":"Poisonous Spillbug","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:poisonous-spillbug","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"None","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Swamp","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"+3 Energy damage","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"10 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR III p. 344","description":"This is a species similar to a bug, with a total length of more than 1 meter. It prefers moist ground, such as swamps and deep forests where there is no sunlight. It constantly secretes poisonous body fluid, which it uses to weaken approaching small animals and prey on them.\n\nIts poisonous shell can become a dangerous weapon if carefully processed and traded at a high price by some.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Corrosive Fluid Secretion","description":"If the monster is hit by a melee or ranged attack, the weapon or ammunition will be affected by the corrosive fluid. If not cleaned with at least 1 liter of alcohol within 24 hours, they will rot and become useless. Magic weapons and ammunition are not affected by this effect.\nIf the attack was made with a natural weapon, the attacker must suffer 1d poison magic damage for each hit."},{"title":"► Venom Spray/5 (12)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Sprays poison fluid at \"Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5\" with \"Range: Caster.\" The target receives 2d poison magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"⏩ Curl Up","description":"It curls up its body and defends itself with its outer shell. While curled up, it gains +3 Defense points but cannot make a melee attack with its Mouth.\nStretching a curled up body is also a Minor Action. The body can only be curled up or stretched before the Major Action is executed.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 11 |\nPoisonous Shell (250G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nHighly Poisonous Shell (750G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Poisonous Spillbug","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lzw9aSCZkwasxFS2","name":"Lizard Fly","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lizard-fly","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"None","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Deserts","reputation":9,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"+3 Energy damage","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"10 (many legs) / 17 (flying)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR III p. 344","description":"Lizard Flies appear to be larger than average lizards, ranging in size from about 50cm to 1m, with two pairs of thin, translucent wings on their back.\n\nCarnivorous, they will stay buried under sand until prey comes near, then spring out and attack.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Lizard Fly receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSand Lizard Skin (70G/Red B) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 11 |\nThin Wings (120G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nGlittering Feathers (340G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lizard Fly","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"m91wATSb9P0JChjv","name":"Warble Crow","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:warble-crow","level":5,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands, Mountains","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"- / 20 (Flying)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"BM","description":"A large crow-like bird with a height of 50 cm and a wingspan of 1m 50cm. They are highly intelligent for animals and have been tamed by the Bolg . In addition to being used as a combat force, they can be given courier missions or conduct simple reconnaissance.\n\nWhen it finds a Humanoid, it makes \"Caw, caw\" sounds to alert Barbarous at a distance.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Warble Crow receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Tear Off","description":"If the result of the damage roll is 4 or less, discard the result and reroll 2d to determine damage again. This effect is only valid once per damage roll.\nThis ability has no effect on characters equipped with metal armor or characters with special abilities such as [Stone Body] that prevent critical hits with edged weapons.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nGouging Beak (220G / Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Warble Crow","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"nXvVPaAWZ5FDCHaL","name":"Roc","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:roc","level":14,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":25,"movementSpeed":"15/60(Flying)","fortitude":"19 (26)","willpower":"17 (24)","source":"CR III p. 353","description":"A monstrous bird whose wingspan reaches 30m, the Roc is a wondrous sight to see. They live in the higher altitudes of most mountain ranges, though their massive form and vivid coloring can be seen from quite far away. With their massive talons, they can grab even mature cows and fly away with them, let alone a full-grown humanoid.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Roc successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target.\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • Impossible","description":"The huge Roc's Body hinders attacks.\nThe Head of the Roc cannot be attacked with melee and ranged attacks. This unique skill is lost when the Body section has 0 or less HP.\nWing"},{"title":"► Windstorm/18 (25)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"The Roc flaps its wings, creating high winds dealing 2d+12 physical damage within \"Range: Caster\" to \"Target: All Areas (30m Radius) / All\".\nTo use this ability, both Wing sections must be ready for Major Action. Also, when this ability is used, the Major Action of both Wing sections is completed.\nThis unique skill cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"All sections receive a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nThis unique skill is lost if the Wing sections are reduced to 0 or less HP.\nLeg"},{"title":"◯ Clutch","description":"If the Talon attack hits, the target is grabbed; the target can no longer move and can only perform melee attacks against the Leg that is grabbing it.\nRoc cannot attack the target Leg has grabbed except with the section it has grabbed ([ ► Windstorm] also cannot hit the target). However, the Talons of Leg section will automatically hit.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use the de-bonding rules. If the monster itself wants to release the target, it can do so with a Minor Action.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nStrange Flight Feathers (500G/Red A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 12 |\nBeautiful Feathers (1,200G/Gold Red S) |\n13+ |\nVivid Feathers (3,000G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Roc","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"nYilCby0lJIx1POV","name":"Fake Angler","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:fake-angler","level":8,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Oceans","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage + 3","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"7(Crawling)/15(Swimming)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"KF","description":"A giant anglerfish, about 5 to 7 meters long, it can be found in the coastal areas of the Alframe continent.\n\nOn its back are piles of ruins and building junk, which at night or from a distance may appear to be island structures.\n\nAmong the Barbarous, the Lizardmen are particularly knowledgeable about the ecology of this monster, and there are reports that they treat it as a nest or base, or use it to approach the coast.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"◯ Natural Mimicry/16/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"The Fake Angler disguises itself as an island by floating with only its back breaching the surface of the water. While it is using this mimicry, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster. If a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with Target Number 16, and if it fails, they will be surprised (see CR I, p. 144). Mimicry will be automatically ended once the monster starts to act.\nThis monster cannot be detected with [ Sense Magic ].\nHead"},{"title":"► Dizzying Light/10 (17)/Willpower/Negates","description":"Within \"Range: Caster,\" it shines a lantern on the forehead and confuses \"Target: All Areas (30m Radius) / All\".\nThe target will appear to be out of position or distance from all characters, including Fake Angler, for 10 seconds (1 round), and when attempting to use a ranged attack or ranged effect, the target must roll 1d after determining the target, and if the roll is 1 or 2, the target cannot be properly targeted, and the action must be canceled. If canceled, any ammunition, MP, and consumables will not be lost (though the target forfeits their action for the turn).\nEvery time this effect is used, it costs 10 points of MP.\nThis effect is Psychic type.\nBack"},{"title":"◯ Spine Fin Poison/11 (18)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"A target hit by a Spine Fin attack and suffering from more than 1 point of applied damage to HP will suffer an additional 7 points of poison magic damage.\nTail"},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHuge Lantern (2,000G/Red S) |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nStale Scales (370G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Fake Angler","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"nfw92C2XBTXB4u5O","name":"Grizzly Bear","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:grizzly-bear","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":12,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR III p. 345","description":"A large bear with grey-brown fur, Grizzlies can stand on their hind legs to intimidate would-be predators, standing around 2-3m tall. In the summer, they will rarely appear to those wandering in the wilderness, but as the seasons change, they will attack livestock to build up bulk for their winter hibernation. Grizzlies are especially dangerous during the springtime, as they are ravenously hungry after hibernation.\n\nBear paws, specifically the right paw, are used as ingredients in high-end cuisine, as the right paw is used to scoop honey. It is said that honey has infused itself into the bear's skin, giving the paw an almost sweet, gamey flavor. The left paw, however, is rarely used and often discarded as there is little demand for it.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Double Attack","description":"A Grizzly Bear can make two Claw attacks."},{"title":"◯ Bear Hug","description":"If both attacks with [ ► Double Attack] hit, the Grizzly Bear will hold the target, and the target will not be able to move or make melee or ranged attacks. Each round, the held target is hit automatically by the Grizzly Bear, dealing 2d + 16 damage.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use the de-bonding rules.\nWhile entangled by this unique skill, the Grizzly Bear cannot attack other characters. If the monster itself wants to release the target, it can do so with a Minor Action."},{"title":"🗨 Power Attack","description":"They can deal an additional +4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nFur (150G/Red A) |\n2 - 12 |\nBear Paws (300G/Red A) |\n13+ |\nAromatic Bear Paws (1,200G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Grizzly Bear","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"nj5IeGFlj7nuBSxP","name":"Lunoicos","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lunoicos","level":13,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Plain","reputation":17,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Energy damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"17 (24)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR III p. 352","description":"A giant reptile which walks on all four legs, covered with glowing scales. The glowing effect is believed to be created by microscopic insects living symbiotically on the body's surface. They receive nutrients from the main body of Lunoicos and protect them from approaching foreign enemies by strongly glowing.\n\nLunoicos themselves are herbivores and do not actively attack other organisms. However, they have learned to harness the power of their symbionts and tend to confront danger rather than flee from it.\n\nAfter the death of the Lunoicos, the symbionts reduce their activity to an extremely low level to survive. The scales become pale and luminescent, which lasts for a long time. This makes them highly prized as accessory materials. Each individual has a slight difference in the light's hue, making it collectible to enthusiasts.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Light Protection","description":"It protects itself with a light covering its entire body. A character who makes a melee attack against this monster, regardless of success or failure, suffers 6 Energy fixed damage for each attempt.\nThis monster illuminates an area of 2 to 3 areas (10m Radius) centered on itself.\nHead"},{"title":"► Light Ray/16 (23)/Fortitude/Half","description":"It attacks by firing a huge beam of energy light from its horns.\nWith \"Range/Area: 2 (30m)/ Line \" dealing 2d+12 energy magic damage.\nThis effect cannot be used on consecutive turns.\nFront &amp; Back"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • +4","description":"The Head cannot be attacked in melee. Against any ranged attacks, Head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks.\nThis effect disappears when either Front or Back section falls to 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +12 points.\nTail"},{"title":"🗨 Tail Swing","description":"The monster can use its Tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nFaintly Glowing Scale (370/Gold Red A) |\n5 - 9 |\nGlowing Blue Scale (670G/Gold Red A) |\n10+ |\nWhite Green Scales (3,370G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lunoicos","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"o27svsiypIsWphLh","name":"Hydra","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hydra","level":11,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Lakes, Swamps","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"12 (Crawling)/12(Swimming)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II, p. 362","description":"A Hydra is a beast with numerous snake-heads, about 10 meters long. Each head has an independent ego and each prey on instinct. They usually emerge from swamps and lakes and attack animals in the lakeshore with only their heads protruding. The number of heads of a Hydra is often reported to be 7-9, but various accounts suggest that the number may vary, and each individual is thought to have a different number of heads.\n\nWhen the body is attacked, all heads concentrate on this enemy. Hydras have exceptional regeneration ability. It is said they are able to revive heads repeatedly unless the wound is burned.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hydra","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"oG9eiyieYN8sF4hn","name":"Cetus","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cetus","level":10,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Lakesides, Oceans","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"18 (Crawling) / 27 (Swimming)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 124","description":"This is a giant aquatic animal with a dog-like head and a whale-like body. The adult's total length exceeds 10m, and it has fin-like limbs, allowing it to move on land as well. It sweeps away enemies with its tail fin and spits water breath. Also, when underwater, it creates large waves to attack enemies on the sea surface or at the water's edge.\n\nThis beast claims lakes and seas as its territory, occasionally appearing on the shore. They are voracious creatures, and consider anything that moves to be prey, so they often attack boats or people walking near the water.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":"There are no restrictions or penalties for actions in water."},{"title":"◯Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Attitude Control","description":"Does not fall prone under any effect."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"When the HP of Head section falls to 0 or less, if either Right Body or Left Body section has 1 or more HP, the loot of the \"Giant Body Spine\" will be lost.\nHead"},{"title":"►Water Blade Breath / 13 (20) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Spits out a sharp stream of water from the mouth to attack. Deals 2d+14 points of Water/Ice and Slashing-type magic damage with \"Range/Area: 2(30m)/ Line \". This ability cannot be used in consecutive turns.\nRight Body/Left Body"},{"title":"►Kicking Spray / 12 (19) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Violently moves its fins, pushing with the flow of water. Targets within \"Range: Caster\" and \"Radius 6m (1 area)/All\" take 2d+18 points of physical damage. Furthermore, targets that fail their resistance check are knocked prone.\nThis ability cannot be used unless the Right Body and Left Body sections have not yet acted, and using it will mark both sections as having acted. Additionally, this ability can only be used when the user is underwater or in a body of water deep enough to submerge up to their knees."},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = Impossible・+4","description":"Its size hinders attacks. Head section cannot be targeted by Melee Attacks, and gains a +4 bonus to Evasion against Ranged Attacks.\nThis effect is lost if either Right Body or Left Body section HP drops to 0 or below."},{"title":"◯Supporting Massive Body","description":"By using disabled sections as a foundation for weight shifting, other sections can perform actions more easily.\nIf either Right Body or Left Body section HP drops to 0 or below, all remaining sections gain a +1 bonus to Melee Attack Accuracy checks and increase damage by +3 points.\nThis effect is lost if both the Right Body and Left Body sections' HP drop to 0 or below.\nTail Fin"},{"title":"🗨Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. Accuracy checks are done on all of them at once, and if multiple characters are hit, damage is determined individually.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"🗨All-Out Attack","description":"A Tail Fin can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGiant Body Spine (6,000G/Red S) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 12 |\nRough Outer Skin (800G/Red A) x 1d |\n13+ |\nRough Outer Skin (800G/Red A) x 2d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cetus","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ofMCIJ4mfwsNRnY5","name":"Sky Whale","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sky-whale","level":10,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"Sea Animal","habitat":"Mountains, Floating Masses","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Wind damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Floating)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II p. 361","description":"These flying whales live in the vicinity of the Floating Masses. They are white and can grow up to 15 meters in length. They usually hide among clouds and are not easily spotted.\n\nThey prey on small flying birds and rarely attack Humanoids.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Sky Whale (mount).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite(Head)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":96,"max":96},"mp":{"value":33,"max":33}},{"style":"Slam(Body)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":88,"max":88},"mp":{"value":31,"max":31}},{"style":"Tail(Tail)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":68,"max":68},"mp":{"value":25,"max":25}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"►Ultrasonic Attack/12 (19)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Shot\", the target is hit with a highly directional ultrasonic blast that paralyzes the enemy. Target will have -2 on all action checks for 30 seconds (3 rounds). This effect is not cumulative.\nA character who is deafened is immune to this effect."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"►Mist Breath/13 (20/Fortitude/Half","description":"With \"Range/area: 2 (20m)/ Shot\" and \"Target: 1 area (5m Radius) / 15\" is dealt 2d+12 water/ice magic damage.\nIn addition, a target that fails a resistance check suffers a -2 penalty on Accuracy checks and Evasion checks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Tail","description":""},{"title":"🗨Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Water Crystal (1,600G/Gold S)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Wind Crystal (1,600G)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sky Whale","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"op2R5vMOlR1QnOaq","name":"Cotton Crown","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cotton-crown","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":10,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 121","description":"Cotton Crowns are very similar to Pamana Bees , with the only difference being the presence of white cotton wool on their heads. This cotton wool is actually a parasitic fungus that infects the Pamana Bee.\n\nWhen parasitized, Pamana Bees become aggressive and start feeding on meat to gather more nutrients. Even the normally docile worker bees, except for the Nest Guards, begin to attack other creatures indiscriminately.\n\nParasitized bees often become solitary and rarely return to the nest. However, in some cases, they do return and contaminate the entire hive. This leads to the production of a large number of Cotton Crowns, which aggressively consume and destroy the surrounding ecosystem.\n\nFortunately, the range of the Cotton Crown is limited to less than one kilometer in radius, compared to the original Pamana Bee. In addition, as the fungus-infested Queens lose their ability to lay eggs, the number of infected hives gradually decreases over time.\n\nThe mycelium of this fungus is prized as a material for \"Cotton Crown Cushions\" (see Natural History of Burlight p. 42). Some people even risk their lives to venture into the prairie in search of Cotton Crowns, often accompanied by the search for Pamana Bee nests.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Fire Vulnerability","description":"When the Cotton Crown is hit by Fire-type damage, it takes an extra 3 points of damage."},{"title":"◯Flight","description":"A Cotton Crown receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯Poison / 6 (13) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If a Poison Stinger attack hits and deals 1 or more points of applied damage, the target is dealt an additional 8 Poison magic damage."},{"title":"◯Disease Spores / 5 (12) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"Whenever this monster receives more than 1 point of applied damage to HP, except Fire type, it sprays spores that cause disease within \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: 1 area (3m radius) / All\". All targets must perform Fortitude Checks immediately. If failed, the target's maximum and current values of HP and MP are both reduced by 3 points (not less than 0). This effect is cumulative, and a character whose maximum HP falls to 0 will die immediately without making a Death Check.\nThis effect is treated as Disease type and does not heal on its own. When curing with the [ Cure Disease ] spell, the spell's Success Value must be compared to the initial attack score."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"|"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"|"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cotton Crown","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"oz7Tru0FKXJmir96","name":"Gluttony Sandworm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gluttony-worm","level":7,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Hearing Only)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Deserts","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"25 (Crawling)/25 (Underground)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Ancient Blue (SW2.5 supplement), p. 135","description":"Said to be either a Sandworm that has grown huge over many years, or a mutated form. While boasting a massive body over 10m in length, the Gluttony Sandworm burrows underground and waits for prey to pass overhead, then suddenly emerges to swallow them whole from beneath their feet.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Mimicry / 14 / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"Uses mimicry in the dunes. While using Mimicry, Monster Knowledge checks cannot be made against this monster. If approached carelessly, make a Danger Sense check against Target Number 14, and if failed, suffer a surprise attack (see CR I, p. 144). When it acts, Mimicry is automatically canceled."},{"title":"◯Insatiable Gluttony","description":"When faced with mortal danger, it goes berserk, trying to devour everything around it, driven by rage and survival instinct.\nAfter the Front section's HP falls to 30 or below at the start of its turn, both the Front and Back section's Damage and Defense increase by 4 points. This effect continues until HP recovers above 31 or falls to 0 or below."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"The \"Glutton's Liver\" loot can only be obtained when reducing the Front section's HP to 0 or below while the [◯Insatiable Gluttony] effect is active."},{"title":"◯Attitude Control","description":"Immune to all effects that would cause it to fall prone."},{"title":"◯Earth Immunity","description":"Front"},{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Mouth attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯Swallow Whole","description":"After normal damage resolution, targets hit by the Mouth attack are absorbed into this monster's body.\nThe absorbed target cannot take any Major Actions except for \"escape\" on their turn, and cannot move at all. Additionally, they cannot be targeted by melee attacks from other characters or effects with \"Range: Touch.\"\nTo \"escape,\" make a check using \"Adventurer Level + Strength modifier\" as the Standard Value against Target Number 14. On success, they escape from the body, but on failure, they remain inside.\nWhen an absorbed target ends their turn inside this monster's body, they take 1d-1 (minimum 0) points of fixed damage.\nWith this effect, up to 2 targets (2 sections) can be absorbed simultaneously. Even if additional mouth attacks hit, no more targets can be absorbed into the body.\nRear"},{"title":"⏩Dust Cloud / 8 (15) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"Within \"Range: Caster\", kicks up sand in the surrounding area. Targets within \"Target: 1 area (5m radius) / All\" receive a -1 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion checks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect can only be used once per round, and when used, it reduces the Rear section's HP by 5 points. This effect is treated as Earth type.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGlutton's Liver (1,200G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nGreen Sandworm Gem (200G/Gold Red A) x 1d |\n9+ |\nGreen Sandworm Gem (200G/Gold Red A) x 2d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gluttony Sandworm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pDI9LrIjM7YbB3pr","name":"Giant Gadfly","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-gadfly","level":1,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Meadow, Swamp","reputation":6,"weakness":9,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"3 (6 Legs)/15 (Flying)","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"CR I p. 410","description":"This is a gigantic fly with a body length of over 50 cm. They attack mainly animals, cutting them with their sharp mouthparts and sucking their blood to fill their bellies.\n\nThey frequently act in herds. Such herds tend to target larger objects because of the ease of attacking them as a group.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Constant Attacks","description":"If an attack by a Giant Gadfly is evaded, the next attack by the Giant Gadfly on that target will gain a +1 bonus to the Accuracy checks until end of the monster's turn.\nThis modifier is cumulative for all Giant Gadflies and has no upper limit. However, it is lost once the Giant Gadfly hits or the last Giant Gadfly attack of the round is avoided.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 11 |\nBlackened Compound Eyes (30G/Red B) |\n12+ |\nShiny Compound Eyes (150G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Gadfly","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"rjiDeWpbwHkXuzFQ","name":"Spotted Rhino","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:spotted-rhino","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Riverbanks, Swamps","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)/15 (Swimming)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"BM","description":"This unusual rhinoceros with speckled skin appears in rivers and swamps. The speckled skin is not as hard as that of the common rhinoceros, and it is said that its preference for diving in the water is probably to avoid predators on the ground.\n\nThey are peaceful and will not attack unless there is a reason, but once angered, they can be extremely destructive.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Charge / 7 (14) / Evasion / Negates","description":"The Spotted Rhino runs forward with \"Range/Area: 2(30m) / Breakthrough ,\" dealing 2d+14 physical damage and knocking them prone.\nTo use this ability, the Spotted Rhino must be able to make a Full Move, and all Sections of its body must be capable of making Major Actions. The use of this ability is declared before the movement, and once it has taken place, all Sections are considered to have taken their Major Actions and the Rhino suffers a -4 penalty to its Evasion for the next 10 seconds (1 round).\nBody"},{"title":"► Kick Away / 7 (14) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Kicks \"Target: 1 Character\" at \"Range: Touch\". The target will be moved one area to the rear of the Rhino (Simplified Combat) or 10m in an arbitrarily determined direction (Standard/Advanced Combat). The victim receives 10 falling damage and will be knocked prone."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Spotted Rhino's height prevents enemies from attacking it. Head receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Body section HP falls to 0 or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBroken Horn (80G / Red B) |\n2 - 4 |\nNothing |\n5 - 8 |\nSpotted Skin (190G / Red A) |\n9+ |\nFine Spotted Skin (780G/ Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Spotted Rhino","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"sEgjEUuErNYzjU0r","name":"Culvert Worm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:culvert-worm","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Rivers","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"20(Crawling)/25(Swimming)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"VC","description":"This is a sub-species of the Sandworm . iIs territory includes muddy rivers and dark marshes. They are green and brown in color and move freely through the mud.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":"2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nNothing |\n5 - 8 |\nSandworm Gem (150G/Gold Red A) |\n9+ |\nGreen Sandworm Gem (200G/Gold Red A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Culvert Worm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"slOKfaYPI4VNM63N","name":"Tiger","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tiger","level":5,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forest","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"22 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR III p. 345","description":"A four-legged carnivore with black and orange stripes. A ferocious feline, these large cats are hunting experts alone, hiding with their striped camouflage and striking unexpectedly. Their fur is prized by fashion enthusiasts, and high-quality pelts can fetch a good price at the market.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fast Action","description":"During the first round of combat, if the Tiger wins initiative, it may take two Major Actions that round."},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Tiger successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nLarge Fang (100G/Red A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 12 |\nTiger Pelt (200G/Red A) |\n13+ |\nFine Tiger Pelt (600G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tiger","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tB7uldpvKPvXRaTL","name":"Nailed Snail","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:nailed-snail","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Swamps, Forests","reputation":12,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"8 (Crawling)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla , p. 125","description":"This is a giant snail that inhabits humid wetlands and riverside forests centered around the three great lakes of the Fairy Kingdom Federation Avalf in the Ursyla Region, reaching about 1.5m in shell length alone. Its shell is lined with sharp, rib-like spines that wound anything that comes too close.\n\nWhile it hibernates underwater during winter, it can be spotted away from water sources in other seasons. It is herbivorous and can devastate large amounts of vegetation, even as a single individual. Since it can appear in large numbers during its breeding season every few years, it is considered a threat by the races who protect the forests. It appears to view Meria as prey and actively attacks them.\n\nIts shell is used as a material for crafts. In particular, shells with well-balanced numbers, positions, and growth directions of spines are traded at high prices. Additionally, its meat has little odor and is eaten as \"land shellfish.\"","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Thorn Defense","description":"Any character attempting a melee attack against this monster receives 1 point of fixed damage each time, regardless of whether the attack succeeds or fails."},{"title":"◯Throw","description":"When a Slam attack hits, it knocks the target prone."},{"title":"🗨Spike Strike","description":"Projects all shell spikes forward to perform a devastating attack. The charge attack receives +1 for Accuracy and +3 points for damage. When using this effect, the [◯Thorn Defense] ability is lost for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect cannot be declared in consecutive turns."},{"title":"►Dissolving Mucus Spray / Can't","description":"Using this effect consumes 5 MP points. Sprays a highly viscous liquid that dissolves plants with \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: 1 area (5m radius) / Space\".\nAll characters within the effect area who are grounded and moving receive a -1 penalty for Accuracy and Evasion checks.\nAdditionally, characters who are \"Race: Meria ,\" \"Race: Arbor ,\" or \"Classification: Plant \" take 3 points of Poison fixed damage at the start of their turn. The Nailed Snail itself is not affected by this effect.\nThis effect persists for 3 minutes (18 rounds)."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If defeated while the \"Spike Strike\" effect is active, the loot Spiked Shell cannot be obtained, and all drops are changed to Worthless Shell.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nTender Meat (60G/Red B) |\n2 - 7 |\nWorthless Shell (40G/Red Black B) |\n8+ |\nSpiked Shell (400G/Red Black A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Nailed Snail","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tQevT5g8E27NWcTl","name":"Giant Crab","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-crab","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Coast, Ocean","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"14 (Many Legs)/14 (Swimming)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR II p. 355","description":"Measuring on average 2m, a Giant Crab uses its size, bulk, and powerful pincers to take down their prey. It's even said that some land-based animals have been caught and eaten by Giant Crabs.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"Can make two Pincers attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSharp Pincers (50G/Red B) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11+ |\nCrab Innards (600G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Crab","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"u0g4D0FocsJTyegO","name":"Murder Hornet","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:murder-hornet","level":11,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Grassland","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":21,"movementSpeed":"-/40(Flying)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.121","description":"Enormous bees, each one measuring a staggering 2 meters, roam the forests and grasslands of the northern Alframe continent. These majestic creatures hunt larger animals and build nests so massive that they could easily be mistaken for flying boulders.\n\nSo great is their weight that ancient structures and towering trees alike are said to have collapsed under their burden. But it is not just their size that is awe-inspiring. The needle on their abdomen is equally massive, nearly 20 cm in length, and coated with a deadly poison that can blind with a single touch.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Murder Hornet receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Vital Strike","description":"If the 2d roll determining damage is 9 or more, the damage is increased by +8 points."},{"title":"◯ Deadly Poisonous Needle/14 (21)/Fortitude/Half","description":"If the Needle hits, it deals 2d+6 Poison magic damage."},{"title":"► Murderous Wing Noise/13 (20)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"The Murder Hornet flaps its wings at high speed and sprays deafening noise to \"Target: 2-3 areas (10m radius) / All\" within \"Range: Caster\", which interferes with the concentration. The targets lose their hearing, and at the same time, suffers a -2 penalty to Spellcasting check and action checks.\nThis effect is of Psychic type. It cannot be used for consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nDeadly Poisonous Needle (2,400G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Murder Hornet","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"unjhVEPGgIici5VL","name":"Sideby Cheetah","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sideby-cheetah","level":5,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands, Wastelands","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning Damage +3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"35 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 122","description":"This is a carnivorous beast widely spread across the grasslands and wastelands of the Dorden region. The sight of them running alongside magic-powered trains is common. Most of them run parallel to the train as long as their stamina allows, then leave satisfied, but occasionally they may jump onto the train and attack.\n\nBesides magic-powered trains, when they spot land animals or vehicles moving at high speeds within their territory, such as Mounts , they run alongside them as if to compare speeds.\n\nWhen they get excited or feel like they're about to lose the speed competition, they attack the target. In most such cases, they are already excited, and the [◯Blood Circulation Spots] have already appeared.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Blood Circulation Spots","description":"During prolonged periods of tension, such as high-speed movement or combat, blood flow becomes more active, causing red spots to appear on the body's surface. As time passes, these spots increase in number and change color from vivid red to purple.\nAt the start of its turn, the monster gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks, and damage is increased by +2 points. This effect lasts for 3 minutes (18 rounds), activating at the start of each turn, and can accumulate up to a maximum of +3 to Accuracy checks and +6 to damage.\nWhen this effect is enhancing Accuracy checks and damage, the monster takes 5 points of fixed damage at the end of each turn.\nThis effect is not activated if its HP is 15 points or less at the start of its turn, and all bonuses to Accuracy and damage increase are lost."},{"title":"◯Evasive Stance","description":"If a Melee Attack with Bite is avoided, it gains a +1 bonus to Evasion checks for 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If its HP drops to 0 or less without the effect of increased Accuracy check and damage from the unique skill [◯Blood Circulation Spots], the \"Spotted Fur\" loot is lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSpotted Fur (700G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 11 |\nFang (100G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nSharp Fangs (200G/Red A) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sideby Cheetah","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"wUecZ82ECvtaIgyq","name":"Giant Boar","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:giant-bohr","level":9,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"25 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR III p. 349","description":"These huge boars, which live in forests and mountains and reach more than 5 meters in length, are omnivores and are feared as demolishers of the environment because of their appetite for devouring anything and everything they can find and the wildness that they can rampage about on their huge bodies. They are extremely belligerent and territorial and will react with fierce hostility to anyone who approaches them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Trample","description":"A melee attack is applied to the targets within \"Range/Area: 1 (25m) / Breakthrough \", and a melee attack is applied to each target by any one section of this monster.\nOnce this ability is used, all sections will complete the Major Action.\nThis ability cannot be used if the HP of the Body section is 0 or less.\nBody"},{"title":"► Full Speed Rush","description":"This ability can only be used in a melee.\nGiant Boar rampages around and leaves the melee. It changes position to an adjacent area in the backward direction (Simplified Combat) or to any coordinates within 25m front or back (Standard Combat, Advanced Combat).\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nFur (150G/Red A) |\n5 - 9 |\nFine Fur (450G/Red A) |\n10+ |\nBest Fur (1,350G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Giant Boar","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xBVkBieG7VXs5HGH","name":"Dinos","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dinos","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Cold Region","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"13","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 413","description":"This is a large false dragon, white-scaled, that inhabits the cold regions of the Alframe continent. It is about 3 meters long, with small forelimbs and hindlimbs for body support and a long tail for balance.\n\nIt has an organ that produces cold air in the body and can exhale it.\n\nTheir meat is edible and can be frozen and brought home using its cooling organs, making them the desired target for hunting.\n\nFor the mount version of this creature, see Dinos (mount) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Freezing Breath / 5 (12) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Spits mass of cold air with \"Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot \" at \"Target: 1 Character\", dealing 2d+2 Water/Ice magic damage.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Dinos' height prevents enemies from attacking their heads. The Head section receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nWhen the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nFrozen Meat (90G/Red B) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 12 |\nFalse-dragon Scale (350G/Red A) |\n13+ |\nWater Crystal (1,600G/Gold S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dinos","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xNCx18IIZqtzfMDb","name":"Crimson Maggot","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:crimson-maggot","level":6,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"None","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"10(Crawling)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR III p. 346","description":"This maggot is a larva that has grown to about 1m to 1m 50cm in length without becoming an adult. They are reddish-black in color and move with surprising agility.\n\nIt has a symbiotic relationship with Fossil Chrysalis and preys on small animals that approach it.\n\nIn times of crisis, they tend to eat the allies around them, enhancing their abilities.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity, ◯ Psychic Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Bloodsucking","description":"If a Bite attack hits, the monster's HP is restored by a value equal to the applied damage."},{"title":"► Cannibalism","description":"Within \"Range: Touch,\" this monster preys on other Crimson Maggots with \"Target: 1 Character\".\nThe target dies immediately. At the same time, the monster's HP is restored to its maximum value.\nFor the next 3 minutes (18 rounds), the Crimson Maggot using this effect, gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and +2 points to damage. This effect is cumulative up to 4 times (Accuracy check +4, damage +8)."},{"title":"◯ Splashing Bodily Fluids/Can't","description":"If this monster dies (including when it is targeted by [ ► Cannibalism]), it sprays hot bodily fluids to \"Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5\" at \"Range: Caster\" and deals 1d fire magic damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nReddish Black Body Fluid (70G/Red B) |\n9+ |\nRed Body Fluid (550G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Crimson Maggot","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xxxrAlovo9yHOd7f","name":"Noisy Rattlesnake","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:noisy-rattlesnake","level":9,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Forests, Grassland, Desert","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"14(Crawling)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 359","description":"This type of rattlesnake boasts a vast body that can reach nearly 10 meters in length and a body thickness of over 20 centimeters in diameter. The intimidating sound they make with their tails is so loud that it is said to send anyone who hears it into a panic.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison/11 (18)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Bite attack hits, it deals additional 8 points of poison magic damage to the target."},{"title":"◯ Counter","description":"This is the same effect as the combat feat [ Counter ]."},{"title":"🗨 Strength Burst","description":"It is always ready to make a move. The monster receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and a -1 penalty to Evasion checks until the beginning of its next turn.\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Noise Disturbance/Can't","description":"The sound made by the Tail disturbs mental concentration. The Tail gives a -4 penalty to Spellcasting checks and Performance checks for \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All areas (50m radius)/All\".\nThis effect has \"Resistance: Can't,\" but it does not extend to characters that cannot hear (see CR II, p. 71)."},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Tail attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nRattling Tail (770G/Red A) |\n2 - 4 |\nSnake Skin (20G/Red B) |\n5 - 8 |\nFine Snake Skin (120G/Red A) |\n9+ |\nPremium Snake Skin (320G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Noisy Rattlesnake","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yElPYp2V5re05QWH","name":"Frost Panther","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:frost-panther","level":8,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Cold regions","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"23 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 358","description":"This is a dangerous large predator of the cat family that roams the snowfields. Its pure white fur is almost invisible in the middle of the day. The skin provides more than enough warmth to keep the monster waiting for its prey in the snow for hours.\n\nBecause of its whiteness and warmth, its fur is valuable as the finest clothing material.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Snow and Ice Mastery","description":"On snow and ice, it has no penalties due to poor footing."},{"title":"◯ Mimicry/16/Danger Sense/Negates","description":"It blends its white body into the snowfield. While mimicking, characters cannot perform a Monster Knowledge check on this monster.\nIf a character approaches it unintentionally, they need to make a Danger check with target number 16, and if it fails, they will be surprised (see CR I, p. 144). Mimicry will be automatically ended once the monster starts to act.\nThis monster cannot be detected with [ Sense Magic ]."},{"title":"► Triple Attack","description":"Frost Panther can attack the same target with three attacks.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 12 |\nGlossy Fur (150G/Gold Red A) |\n13+ |\nSnow White Fur (2,600G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Frost Panther","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"z5zLwix7J3F79Ur0","name":"Kidnapper Pelican","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:kidnapper-pelican","level":4,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hungry","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Coasts, Cliffs","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Wind Damage +3","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"7 / 14 (Flying)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 122","description":"This is a terrifying monstrous bird that carries off its prey, such as Animals or Human children, in its enormous beak. If it so desires, it can even capture and carry adult Humans.\n\nThe prey is killed by being dropped from a great height and then used as food. These birds build their nests on steep cliffs along the Sikh Sea coast in the Dorden Region and on nearby islands, targeting isolated villages. When food is plentiful, they sometimes keep their captured prey alive, releasing them near their cliff-side nests.\n\nTheir internal organs, especially the liver, are a well=known delicacy. However, due to the aversion of possibly eating something that has consumed Humanoids, young birds just before they can fly are preferred. There are a fair number of people who, at the request of gourmets seeking this delicacy, venture to target the nests built on the cliffs.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight","description":"A Kidnapper Pelican receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"►Engulf / 5 (12) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Target: one character is placed inside the mouth. The target becomes unable to perform Major Actions other than escape. If attempting to escape, follow the \" de-bonding \" process (see ML, p. 71).\nIf one character has already been engulfed using this ability, no more can be taken into the mouth."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If damage from a blunt weapon reduces its HP to 0 or less, the loot entry Rich Liver will be lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nRich Liver (400G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nFlight Feathers (100G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Kidnapper Pelican","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zXiwW7PD6AZvrJQN","name":"Sandworm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sandworm","level":5,"monsterType":"Animal","intelligence":"Animal","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Desert","reputation":10,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"20 (Crawling)/20 (Burrow)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR I p. 413","description":"A giant snake-like creature that lives in the sand, which may have up to one-fifth of its body covered in a hard exoskeleton. Older Sandworms often have gems in their hide, formed from sand and pressure. The green gems carry a high price in markets, while the clear gems have value when crushed into an abrasive polishing powder.\n\nSome Bolgs have reportedly tamed Sandworms and use them in battle.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sandworm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
